  "term": "biogenic",
  "definition": "Biogenic refers to naturally occurring amine chemicals found in honey bee venom, such as dopamine, norepinephrine, tyramine, and serotonin. In this source, these substances vary with age, caste, nutrition, and social role, and may produce physiological effects in other animals and insects.",
